WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.900
[This film is restricted]

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.800
[War Department, Official Training Film, 
T.F.8 1423, Army Service Forces]

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:14.700
[Produced by Army Pictorial Service
Signal Corps]

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.300
[Easy to Get]

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:24.400
[Music]

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.500
[Narrator:] You're looking at a really happy mister. 

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.000
This is Corporal Baker,
home on his first furlough in over a year.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.600
He's a smart, clean-cut guy, and he's a good soldier.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.000
He's going to enjoy these days with his family.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.800
Right now, it's a good, warm feeling walking down Main Street,

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:48.400
exchanging nods and handshakes with the people
who've known him since he was a kid.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.200
Baker would never get by without a visit to the old drugstore,

00:00:54.600 --> 00:01:00.600
for a Coke and a little chatter with anyone who might be around,
just like the days before he went in the Army.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:12.200
 Ah! It's good to be home; sleeping late, no details,
no formations, no marching, taking it easy.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.400
Money on the hip. Faces that he knows. 

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:21.200
Mm, what's this? One that he doesn't know.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:28.400
[Music]

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.400
Now this looks like a girl a man could go for.
Not just for the fun, but for keeps.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.400
If only he could get to talk to her.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.200
Well, he could.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:45.000
It wasn't hard because she wanted a straw
and it happened they were right in front of him.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.600
And that's the way it all started.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.800
It was a nice beginning,
but it was only the beginning.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:59.000
She put the finishing touch to Baker's furlough
and made it wonderful.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.000
She was all that a man dreams about,
gentle and clean.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:11.400
She liked the simple things. Baker did, too.
She didn't drink. She didn't like juke joints.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:16.200
She lived on the next block.
Her mother and father were good people.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.000
She talked soft and she seemed well-educated, like Baker. 

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.500
He enjoyed every moment they spent together. 

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:31.500
You can't blame Baker for enjoying
those moments, especially since she loved him.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:32.800
She told him so.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:57.400
[Music]

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:03.000
Yep, it was a wonderful furlough
and it was tough it ever had to end.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.800
But you know how the Army is about those things.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:11.800
They were going to write each other often,
though, and that would take some of the edge off being apart.

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.000
You sure were lucky, Corporal Baker. 

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:22.800
And all because a sweet girl came along
and wanted a straw for her Coke. 

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:27.200
Well, sit back, Corporal Baker, and have a good time while you can.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.600
Sit there and dream about the ten days you had in heaven. 

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:38.000
Because in a few hours, you're going to find out just what
sort of a furlough you really had.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.600
 [Music]

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.600
Yep, ten wonderful days in heaven.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:50.100
[Dramatic music]

00:03:50.100 --> 00:04:01.000
[Doctor looking through a microscope hands a slide to a technician and then enters his office and sits down.]

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.000
[Doctor:] You've got gonorrhea, Baker.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:09.000
[Corporal Baker:] Gonorrhea? Why, I don't know how -

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.400
[Doctor:] I do. You had a dirty woman.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:15.600
[Corporal Baker:] No, sir. A girl back home.
She wasn't any prostitute.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.800
[Doctor:] Have you known her long?

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.440
[Corporal Baker:] Why I met her the day I got home, sir.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.600
[Doctor:] On the street or in a bar?

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:26.600
[Corporal Baker:] I don't mess around with streetwalkers.
I met her in the drugstore.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:27.800
[Doctor:] Was she a pick-up?

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.900
[Corporal Baker:] No, sir. I just met her, that's all.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.000
[Doctor:] And you had her that night?

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.300
[Corporal Baker:] No, sir. The next night.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:37.800
[Doctor:] And you didn't use a rubber?

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.600
[Corporal Baker:] She was afraid of them, sir.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:42.400
[Doctor:] Or a Pro-Kit?

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:44.800
[Corporal Baker:] No, sir.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.100
[Doctor:] And you didn't go to a pro-station?

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.900
[Corporal Baker:] She looked clean, sir. 
She looked clean all over.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:55.200
[Doctor:] Not on the inside, Corporal. 
Where you touched her she was filthy and diseased.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.400
That girl of yours was just a pick-up.

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:02.400
[Narrator:] Just what does it mean to have gonorrhea? 

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:09.000
Well, take this man. He used to be a star athlete. 

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.200
He caught gonorrhea and went to a drugstore
instead of a medical doctor.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:17.400
Don't you take chances on being crippled like this. 

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.400
And this is the kind of thing gonorrhea means. 

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.200
Furthermore, it doesn't feel any better than it looks.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:32.800
Now, some dumb Joes think gonorrhea is caused by a strain,

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.400
like lifting the rear-end of a Jeep

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.800
or getting tired on a long march.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:41.200
Or knocking yourself out on KP.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:46.600
Or sliding into second. Well, that's plain crazy.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:52.000
The only strain that gives you gonorrhea
is the strain of chasing after a woman.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.800
Well, you know what Corporal Baker's doing here
in the dispensary waiting for treatments.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.400
What's this other guy doing here?

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:04.400
He's Private Anderson,
in the same outfit as Baker's.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:09.000
He's more of a playboy than Baker, but he's not a bad soldier.

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:12.600
He's just out for the laughs, and the more of them the better.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.960
He looks pretty unhappy right now, 

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.000
but imagine it's a week earlier.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.000
He didn't look so unhappy then.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:28.200
He'd just been paid and tonight he's going
to cut himself a slice of good time. 

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:32.000
 Anderson's idea of a good time is drinking and girls.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:36.600
He's had months of marching and KP
and this is his night to howl.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:39.400
Well, the prophylactic station's handy.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.600
He'll be coming back here for a pro after he's had his fun.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:50.000
Sure, Anderson will be stopping in at the pro-station.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:55.600
Or, anyway, that's what he thinks now, 
while he's sober and can still think,

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:58.400
which isn't for long in joints like this one.

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:04.000
See the whole set-up?
Girls, a jukebox, and a bar. 

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:08.900
Especially the bar,
with lots of liquor to lift you until you're way up in the clouds.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:28.600
[Music]

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:33.600
Anderson was definitely out for a good time,
but he didn't think he'd run into anything this good.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:36.400
She certainly was good-looking.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:40.800
Mm, damn sight better looking than any 
he expected to find in a place like this.

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:50.800
 [Music]

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:53.400
Sure, he knew she was a whore. So what?

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:56.200
Whores are supposed to keep clean, aren't they? 

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:00.600
Don't lots of places even have laws to make them keep clean?

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:32.200
[Music and dancing.]

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:46.000
[The soldier and the woman walk upstairs.]

00:08:46.000 --> 00:09:22.200
[The dancing continues.]

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:28.200
[Music]

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:31.400
Now that's what Anderson calls having a good time. 

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:37.000
And when it was over, it was time to take a pro
because it's no good unless you take it right away.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.600
But Anderson didn't exactly feel like leaving.

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:45.000
Not when he could lie around, have a smoke, and

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:48.400
then maybe, for another two bucks,

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:51.600
well, he was out for a good time, wasn't he?

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:57.029
And that's just what he was going to get.
And maybe a little more he wasn't out for.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:03.259
[Doctor:] What made you think she might be
clean, Anderson? She was a prostitute.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:09.709
[Private Anderson:] Well, that's it, sir. I figured
if being a prostitute was her job, she'd have to keep clean.

00:10:09.709 --> 00:10:11.540
[Doctor:] Well, maybe she'd like to,

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.600
 but she can't if she takes on men one after another.

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:19.000
Any man with a couple of dollars.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:21.540
[Private Anderson:] But she had a card that
said she was in good health.

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:23.200
[Doctor:] Probably a week old. 

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:28.400
But even if it had been only an hour old, it still wouldn't mean a thing.

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:35.000
She could've had a man with VD five minutes before she had you
and pass his germs onto you.

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:36.400
[Private Anderson:] Yes, sir.

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:43.400
[Doctor:] You know, you might've stayed well
if you'd gone to the pro station.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:45.000
[Private Anderson:] I will next time, sir.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:48.400
[Doctor:] There won't be any next time for quite awhile, Anderson.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:51.000
You've got syphilis.

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:54.100
[Narrator:] Sweat it out, Anderson.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.600
But if it's any comfort to you, you're lucky.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:02.800
Some men aren't smart enough to go to a doctor when they get a case.

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:10.000
This man, for example.
He was a hero in the last war, 

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:17.500
but the wounds that have kept him in and out of the hospital
ever since 1918 weren't from combat.

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:22.800
He caught syphilis from a whore overseas and
he never went on sick call. 

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:27.400
This man looks as healthy as anybody, 

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:33.600
but the little syphilis germs have been making his blood bad,
and boring into his heart for a long time.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:37.500
 And one day, the heart just quits.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:40.200
[Music]

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:46.600
Yes, he looked healthy, but that's because
syphilis doesn't do much advertising.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:50.800
Take a look at this one. He's really blown his top.

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:54.600
When he talks, he doesn't make much sense, 

00:11:55.400 --> 00:12:00.600
and sometimes he runs wild and has to be held in bed
with straps so he won't hurt anyone.

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:03.800
The syphilis germs got into his brain.

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:05.800
[Doctor:] Is your memory all right?

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:10.400
[Man:] Sure. Remember anything that ever happen.

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:15.600
[Doctor:] Let me test your memory by giving
you three words to remember.

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:21.000
The words are "pink," "Broadway," and "forty-six."

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:24.000
[Man:] Pink, Broadway, forty-six.

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:26.200
[Doctor:] I'll ask you what they were in a moment. 

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:32.600
Is your speech all right? Any, do you stumble over big words? 

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:33.400
[Man] Huh?

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:39.000
[Doctor:] Say after me, "Third riding artillery brigade."

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:42.400
[Man:] Third riding artillery brigade.

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:43.500
[Doctor:] Say it again.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:48.000
[Man:] Third riding artillery brigade. Third riding artillery brigade.

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:52.000
[Doctor:] That's enough.
Now what are the three words that I asked you to remember?

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:56.400
[Man:] I don't know. Pink - 

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:58.800
I can't remember.

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:07.400
[Narrator:] This poor fellow's in mighty bad shape.
And all because of...[dramatic background music]

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:09.700
[VD...Venereal Disease]

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:17.600
There are several venereal diseases, but the
most common two are syphilis and gonorrhea.

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:25.200
Some people call syphilis "bad blood," "pox,"
"lues," "a case," "the dogs," and so on.

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:31.200
Some people call gonorrhea "the clap," "the
strain," "the running range," "a dose."

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:36.400
They all mean venereal disease, VD.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:40.800
It's a bad deal and it's catching. 

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:44.200
And you catch it only one way: from a woman.

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:49.000
It doesn't matter if she's a high school girl or a juke joint girl.

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:53.400
Inside her, there may be sores full of crawling little germs, 

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:58.200
like these wiggling syphilis germs that stick to your skin like molasses.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:03.600
You get these germs and the gonorrhea germs only from a woman.

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:08.200
But you don't get them if you use a condom, a rubber, 

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:13.200
and if you put it on before you even touch a girl.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:18.800
Remember, if she tells you she doesn't want to use a rubber,
she's up to no good.

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:25.500
If she's afraid it might come off and get inside her someplace
so that she'll need an operation to get it out, 

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:26.800
she's just crazy.

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:31.200
Even if you tried, you couldn't force it inside
any place where it could do harm.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:34.400
So don't let any woman talk you out of using one. 

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:42.900
The next best thing is to take a pro at the pro station, 
but take it as soon as possible after you've had your piece.

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:47.200
The way they do it now, it doesn't hurt and
it doesn't take more than a few minutes.

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:50.800
It's a fine way not to catch VD.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:56.500
There's been talk by some stupid guys that
a pro destroys your manhood 

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:59.800
and if you have too many of them,
you won't be able to have sex anymore.

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:03.200
Well, anybody who thinks that is just ignorant.

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:06.800
A pro doesn't hurt anything except germs.

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:12.800
Another good way not to get VD is to use the
Army's new Pro-Kit.

00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:15.800
It was thought up just for men in the Army and it works.

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:23.600
 It consists of a tube of ointment, a soap cloth, 
a piece of tissue, and some instructions.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:26.000
Now, here's all you have to do:

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:31.800
right after you've had sex,
take a leak and wash yourself with the soap cloth.

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:37.600
Then, take the top off the tube
and squeeze one-fourth of it inside.

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:40.500
It doesn't hurt and it doesn't sting. You can't even feel it. 

00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:44.600
Squeeze the rest of the tube onto your fingers and rub it all over.

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:49.600
It kills syphilis and gonorrhea before they
can get started doing their damage. 

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:58.200
Well, those are the ways of keeping clean:
a condom, a rubber, the pro station, and the Pro-Kit.

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:04.000
But the simplest and best way of all is to
stay away from women. 

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:10.200
Your Army doctors know VD. So do your officers and non-coms.

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:14.200
Listen to them when they teach you about syphilis and gonorrhea.

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:15.800
They're trying to help you.

00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:19.400
They want us to become the healthiest people in the world.

00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:23.600
Don't be afraid to go on sick call as soon as you think you've caught VD.

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:27.400
Don't be afraid and don't be ashamed.

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:32.400
You won't be punished.
No gigs, no loss of pay, no loss of rank.

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:38.700
All the Army wants to do is cure you
and send you back to civilian life healthier than you've ever been.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:40.500
You must keep yourself clean. 

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:49.400
Keeping clean means keeping healthy and it was good health
that beat the Germans before the war even started.

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:54.000
This is Joe Louis taking a few pokes at Hitler's boy, Max Schmeling.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:58.800
All of Joe's training was to get him in proper condition, proper health.

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:04.200
This massacre you're looking at couldn't have
taken place if Joe hadn't kept himself clean.

00:17:04.300 --> 00:17:15.079
[Crowd cheering]

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:20.600
Remember the last Olympic Games in Berlin, back in '36? 

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:26.700
A lot of our boys invaded Germany long before the first 
American soldier went down to the Induction Center,

00:17:27.490 --> 00:17:31.400
 and they all knew the value of good health and of staying clean.

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:37.800
There was Owens in the dashes and broad jump,

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:42.600
and Johnson in the high jump.

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:50.100
[Crowd cheers]

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:52.600
And Woodruff and Edwards in the 800 meters.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:03.000
And Ralph Metcalfe was one of the men 
who helped pile up our big score.

00:18:04.300 --> 00:18:06.400
Here he is now in a little bit of a hurry.

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:12.700
Metcalfe sent the Stars and Stripes up above
the Swastika and Rising Sun so often

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:18.300
that Hitler and Hirohito should've taken the hint right there and quit.

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:20.600
And here's Lieutenant Ralph Metcalfe himself.

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:26.500
[Ralph Metcalfe:] Winning a race against tough competition means 
more than just being fast just being fast on your feet.

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:32.100
It's training off of the field as well as
on that gives you that extra speed when you need it most.

00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:34.100
I figure that life's that way, too.

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:39.600
The drive that helps you to break a record
comes from being in shape, perfect shape.

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:45.800
I don't say that I've won races just because
I didn't fool around with women, but it certainly helped.

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:53.600
Remember, military fitness not only includes
technical and mental fitness, but physical fitness as well

00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:56.500
and that means not taking chances with women.

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:59.400
That'll be good for you and for all of us.

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:03.200
[Narrator:] But maybe you don't want to stay
healthy and keep yourself clean.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:07.000
Maybe you want to hop in bed with one gal after another.

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:10.700
Well, maybe you'd like to hop into the same boat with these men. 

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:16.400
This man thought he was killing the VD germs by rubbing whiskey
on his rod after he had a pick-up.

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:20.800
Whiskey doesn't kill anything except the brain.

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:28.400
This man didn't use a rubber
because he'd been told it didn't feel so good with a rubber.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:33.600
Well, what he's got now really doesn't feel good.

00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:41.000
And this man, he had to pay a terrible price for catching syphilis. 

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:44.900
He married the girl he loved and passed the germs onto her.

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:47.500
Pretty soon, she had a baby.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:49.500
It had syphilis, too.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:54.800
[Music]

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:56.600
 It would've been better dead.

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:04.000
This is Paul Robeson, who enjoys the respect
and recognition of the entire world.

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:12.100
From his college days when he was an All-American end
to his great career as singer, actor, and world traveler,

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:16.300
Mr. Robeson has done as
much good for our people as any man alive.

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:17.800
Listen to him

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:21.200
[Paul Robeson:] What you've been seeing here makes a lot of sense. 

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:26.300
Twenty years ago, we didn't have pictures like this.

00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:30.100
For hours, we had to sit and listen to the coach lecture.

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:32.000
He gave it to us hot and heavy and we took it,

00:20:32.300 --> 00:20:36.070
because if you want to play football, 
you've got to have a healthy body.

00:20:36.070 --> 00:20:40.800
In fact, if you want to do anything in this world, 
you've got to have a healthy body.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:44.300
Now this film is pretty frightening,

00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:49.500
yet it's not as frightening as the records 
the War Department has shown me on VD

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:53.000
I tell you, we've got to do something about
this and we have the answer. 

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:56.000
You've seen it right here in this picture.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:21:01.000
None of us will forget what we've learned
from this movie, but more important, 

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:07.600
let's not forget our responsibility to our communities,
our families, and ourselves.

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:10.000
We must defeat VD.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:13.000
[Music]

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:21.400
[The End. T.F. 8 1423]

00:21:22.600 --> 00:21:27.000
[This film is restricted.]

